  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q15.c ****  *
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q15.c ****  * \par
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q15.c ****  * This fast version uses a 32-bit accumulator with 2.30 format.
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q15.c ****  * The accumulator maintains full precision of the intermediate multiplication results but provides
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q15.c ****  * There is no saturation on intermediate additions.
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q15.c ****  * Thus, if the accumulator overflows it wraps around and distorts the result.
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q15.c ****  * The input signals should be scaled down to avoid intermediate overflows.
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q15.c ****  * Scale down one of the inputs by 1/min(srcALen, srcBLen) to avoid overflow since a
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q15.c ****  * maximum of min(srcALen, srcBLen) number of additions is carried internally.
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q15.c ****  * The 2.30 accumulator is right shifted by 15 bits and then saturated to 1.15 format to yield the 
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q15.c ****  *
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q15.c ****  * \par
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q15.c ****  * See <code>arm_correlate_q15()</code> for a slower implementation of this function which uses a 6
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_fast_q15.c ****  */
